// One division per case, labelled with whether it should produce a flag.
//
// The first two are the pair that proves the design works: an identical assessment profile
// at impact class 4 and at impact class 1. If they ever come out the same, the exposure
// normalisation has stopped working and the agent is comparing divisions with each other -
// which is the failure ADR-009 exists to prevent, and it would be invisible in an aggregate
// accuracy number.
//
// The `flagged: false` cases are what make the false-positive rate meaningful. Half this
// set is divisions that must NOT be flagged, because a detector that flags everything
// reaches 100% detection and the cost lands on GN officers in the divisions that were hit
// hardest.
